{
  "slug": "enam",
  "name": "Enam",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Persistent memory for Claude Code — at ~350 tokens ambient cost, with no Docker, no API keys, and no MCP servers.\n\nEngram captures your sessions structurally on PreCompact (zero LLM cost), extracts atomic memories via a single lightweight LLM digest (preferences, practices, current context), and  detects emergent patterns from your history — files you always edit together, recurring errors, tool usage anomalies — stored as an auditable Obsidian-compatible wiki.\n\n\nKey features:\n• Per-project handoff notes — at session start you get a narrative message from the last session in this project\n• Atomic UPSERT memories keyed by topic — latest wins, no drift, no embeddings\n• Emergent pattern detection (co-edits, error recurrence, project streaks, tool anomalies)\n• Durable preferences stay global; ephemeral context is scoped per project\n• 4-flag CLI surface: --stats, --query, --memories, --forget\n• Everything local: SQLite at ~/.claude/memory.db, markdown wiki at ~/.claude/patterns/",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 command** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (1): `wherewasi` (Show where you left off in this project (last task + next step), or --reset to clear it)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PreCompact`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install enam@claude-community` from `sebastianbreguel/engram`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
